            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "MUFG in talks for $2.6 billion stake in India's Shriram Finance, Economic Times reports",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "A deal would mark the latest move by a Japanese financial institution to acquire a stake in an Indian firm, following the banking arm of rival Sumitomo Mitsui Financial Group building a 24.2% holding in Mumbai-based Yes Bank.  Facing a shrinking domestic market and years of rock-bottom interest rates, Japan's biggest banks have enthusiastically sought out targets overseas over many years.  MUFG - Japan's largest lender by assets - owns a 23.62% stake in Wall Street investment bank Morgan Stanley.",
